# Evidence behind the account

| Stage | Read the account | Inspect the evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Generation and methods | [Chapter guide](../docs/decisions.md) · [121-topic index](../docs/methodology-index.md) | [Source fingerprints](../docs/coverage.json) |
| Judge profiles | [How the profiles were built](../docs/judges.md) | [23 historical profiles and reading records](../judges/README.md) |
| Midterm, October 7–11 | [Review and diagnostics](../docs/evaluation.md) | [Closure summary](midterm/README.md) · [Original receipt](midterm/FINAL_RECEIPT.json) |
| Five later programs | [After the midterm](../docs/post-midterm.md) | [24 accepted release packages](post-midterm/releases.json) · [Seven manuscript cycles](../essays/post-midterm/README.md) |
| Final selection, step 1 | [22 candidates and their next tasks](../docs/selection.md) | [Selection records and exact versions](final-selection/README.md) |

Copied source files retain their bytes; editorial summaries and path-normalized indexes are labeled separately. [The import manifest](manifest.json) records earlier source paths and hashes. Paths inside historical records identify the local lab archive, so a referenced path is not necessarily a file included in this edition.

The [timeline](../docs/timeline.md) distinguishes the time of a request, research event, archive acceptance, and later export. The [log index](../logs/README.md) leads to the retained conversations and downloadable machine-log bundles.

Run `python3 tools/verify_edition.py` from the repository to check manuscript fingerprints, quoted prompts, dates, selection versions, local links, and archive contents.
